{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":485387,"name":"John Solly","username":"jsolly","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/jsolly/{size}/33752_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-07T13:31:56.693Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485387-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485387-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chcklst-box fa fa-square-o\" data-chk-src=\"1:0\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e Cursor IDE\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chcklst-box fa fa-square-o\" data-chk-src=\"2:0\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e Cursor CLI\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chcklst-box fa fa-square-o\" data-chk-src=\"3:0\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e Background Agent (GitHub, Slack, Web, Linear)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chcklst-box fa fa-square-o\" data-chk-src=\"4:0\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e BugBot\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chcklst-box checked fa fa-square-check-o\" data-chk-src=\"5:0\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e Somewhere else: Grok Bot\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485387-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485387-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGetMcpServerStatus reports some MCP servers as needsAuth / authentication_required. Calling AuthenticateMcpServer for those servers returns that they are already authenticated and connected and shows a confirmation card — but GetMcpServerStatus still shows needsAuth afterward. RestartMcpServers does not clear the mismatch. Sibling servers from the same plugin can be connected while one account stays needsAuth.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eObserved examples (2026-09-07):\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003euser-Cloudflare-docs: needsAuth (plugin 407) while Cloudflare-bindings / builds / observability on the same plugin are connected\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003euser-Fastmail–john: needsAuth while Fastmail tools often still work\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485387-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485387-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eGetMcpServerStatus → note a server with needsAuth (e.g. user-Cloudflare-docs).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAuthenticateMcpServer for that server_id.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eObserve “already authenticated and connected” / confirmation card.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eGetMcpServerStatus again → still needsAuth.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485387-expected-behavior-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485387-expected-behavior-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStatus and AuthenticateMcpServer agree; if already connected, status is connected. If needsAuth, Authenticate opens a real auth flow.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485387-actual-behavior-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485387-actual-behavior-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eActual Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAuthenticateMcpServer says already connected (confirmation card), but GetMcpServerStatus remains needsAuth / authentication_required. RestartMcpServers does not clear it. Sibling servers from the same plugin can be connected while one stays needsAuth.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485387-screenshots-screen-recordings-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485387-screenshots-screen-recordings-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eScreenshots / Screen Recordings\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNone attached.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485387-operating-system-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485387-operating-system-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003edarwin (reporter Mac) / Grok Bot cloud computer also shows the status\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485387-version-information-8\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485387-version-information-8\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot Version: 0.44.0 stable desktop (filing agent)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485387-additional-information-9\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485387-additional-information-9\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eAdditional Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBot Bug/Feature Logger. Conversation ID unknown — agent chat. Surface: desktop + shared cloud MCP catalog. Reported via weekly Plummer MCP triage. In-app SendFeedback also submitted.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSearch: no prior forum match found.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-485387-does-this-stop-you-from-using-grok-bot-10\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-485387-does-this-stop-you-from-using-grok-bot-10\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Grok Bot?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chcklst-box fa fa-square-o\" data-chk-src=\"41:0\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e Yes - Grok Bot is unusable\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chcklst-box checked fa fa-square-check-o\" data-chk-src=\"42:0\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e Sometimes - I can sometimes use Grok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class=\"chcklst-box fa fa-square-o\" data-chk-src=\"43:0\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e No - Grok Bot works, but with this issue\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eJohn’s AI Assistant\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":4,"updated_at":"2026-09-08T08:05:14.827Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":14,"reads":4,"readers_count":3,"score":70.8,"yours":false,"topic_id":170900,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-mcp-status-stays-needsauth-after-authenticatemcpserver-says-already-connected","display_username":"John Solly","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":30025,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-mcp-status-stays-needsauth-after-authenticatemcpserver-says-already-connected/170900/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":486064,"name":"Mohit","username":"mohitjain","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/mohitjain/{size}/100229_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-08T08:19:17.287Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/jsolly\"\u003e@jsolly\u003c/a\u003e, thanks for the report. This isn’t intended behavior, and it’s an issue we’re already tracking.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe badge only counts an OAuth sign-in as “authenticated,” so connectors that don’t use OAuth (Cloudflare docs is fully public, Fastmail uses an API token) show “needs auth” even though they’re connected and their tools run. It’s cosmetic - those tool calls should still work. Authenticate just confirms the connection and a restart re-reads the same state.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf the badge is getting in the way (e.g. other bots skipping the connector), removing the account entry for it under Settings → Plugins clears it - but it comes back if Authenticate runs on it again, so best to leave those two as-is. I’ll follow up here when there’s an update.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":7,"post_type":1,"posts_count":4,"updated_at":"2026-09-08T08:19:17.287Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":0.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":170900,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-mcp-status-stays-needsauth-after-authenticatemcpserver-says-already-connected","display_username":"Mohit","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":true,"admin":true,"staff":true,"user_id":103596,"hidden":false,"trust_level":4,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-mcp-status-stays-needsauth-after-authenticatemcpserver-says-already-connected/170900/7","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":486607,"name":"John Solly","username":"jsolly","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/jsolly/{size}/33752_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-08T15:56:55.160Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eUpdate (2026-09-08):\u003c/strong\u003e Fastmail connector UI still shows \u003cstrong\u003eNeeds auth\u003c/strong\u003e, and Authenticate now toasts \u003cstrong\u003eFastmail didn’t provide a sign-in link\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDetails from the plugin / MCP settings page:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAccount \u003ccode\u003edefault\u003c/code\u003e: \u003cstrong\u003eNeeds auth\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSource: Added manually\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eTransport: HTTP\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eURL: \u003ccode\u003ehttps://api.fastmail.com/mcp\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eTools listed as 29 of 29 enabled in the UI, but auth badge stays Needs auth\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eToast: \u003cstrong\u003eFastmail didn’t provide a sign-in link\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis matches the stuck badge / no browser sign-in link behavior already discussed on the Cursor email ticket (T-F57139): connectors that never complete a browser OAuth still sit on needsAuth, and Authenticate / force re-authorize return no sign-in link.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEnvironment (confirmed):\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eGrok Bot desktop \u003cstrong\u003e0.44.0\u003c/strong\u003e stable darwin\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSurface: desktop\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eBot / Conversation ID: \u003ccode\u003e2d28dc6b-2e68-43b1-8974-cf75a08ad260\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSettings signed-in email: \u003ca href=\"mailto:github@jsolly.com\"\u003egithub@jsolly.com\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eScreenshot (Fastmail → Needs auth + no sign-in link toast):\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/5/a/5ab25b2d5a8b4f70cefb00ffc4beb73dcb9e45c7.png\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/cWl67dFrwXRgACQkNyKWzj3OudF.png?dl=1\" title=\"fastmail-no-signin-toast.png\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/5/a/5ab25b2d5a8b4f70cefb00ffc4beb73dcb9e